I did not add the `last-input` write. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, and the approval does not add a store interface to that grant. Writing to the store would need a `StateHandle<..., read-write>` grant and a `state-rw` import in the world, and I can't add those without changing the declared authority. Once the `with` clause is updated, the write can be added. The output is unchanged. The code below pre-checks each URL's host against the allowlist, so an out-of-grant URL becomes a `fetch-failure` instead of a trap that aborts the whole run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

const ALLOWED_HOSTS: [&str; 4] = [
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

/// Extracts the lowercase host of an http(s) URL, or None if it cannot be parsed.
fn host_of(url: &str) -> Option<String> {
    let rest = url
        .strip_prefix("https://")
        .or_else(|| url.strip_prefix("http://"))?;
    let end = rest
        .find(|c: char| matches!(c, '/' | '?' | '#'))
        .unwrap_or(rest.len());
    let authority = &rest[..end];
    // Userinfo ends at the last '@'; everything after it is host[:port].
    let host_port = authority.rsplit('@').next()?;
    let host = host_port.split(':').next()?;
    if host.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        Some(host.to_ascii_lowercase())
    }
}

fn is_allowed(url: &str) -> bool {
    match host_of(url) {
        Some(host) => ALLOWED_HOSTS.contains(&host.as_str()),
        None => false,
    }
}

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents: Vec<FeedDocument> = Vec::new();
        let mut failures: Vec<FetchFailure> = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if !is_allowed(&url) {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "host not in node grant".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
